      "tactic": "Persistence — Scheduled Task Creation",
      "technique": "T1053.005",
      "what_happened": "At 2026-05-13T08:14:22+0200, Windows Security EID 4698 (Scheduled task created) fired on WIN-ENDPOINT-07. The task name 'Microsoft\\Windows\\EdgeUpdate\\MicrosoftEdgeUpdateTaskMachineCore_20260513_081422' closely mimics the legitimate Microsoft Edge updater path but appends a timestamp suffix — a typosquat designed to blend with real EdgeUpdate tasks. The creating process image was C:\\Windows\\System32\\schtasks.exe with commandLine 'schtasks /create /tn Microsoft\\Windows\\EdgeUpdate\\MicrosoftEdgeUpdateTaskMachineCore_20260513_081422 /tr powershell.exe -NoProfile -NonInteractive -WindowStyle Hidden -EncodedCommand <base64_blob> /sc MINUTE /mo 5 /f'. The task action contains powershell.exe with -EncodedCommand and -WindowStyle Hidden flags — a canonical encoded-payload persistence technique. The schedule is every 5 minutes, consistent with C2 callback keep-alive intervals.",
      "chain_reason": "Wazuh rule 92760 correlated EID 4698 + task name pattern matching EdgeUpdate + task action containing -EncodedCommand. The 3-signal chain (EID 4698 + typosquat task name + encoded PowerShell action) is the canonical T1053.005 TP trigger.",
      "first_seen": "2026-05-13T08:14:22+0200"
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "tactic": "Persistence — Scheduled Task Execution Confirmation",
      "technique": "T1053.005",
      "what_happened": "At 2026-05-13T08:17:08+0200, EID 4702 (Scheduled task updated) fired — the task was queried via 'schtasks /query /tn Microsoft\\Windows\\EdgeUpdate\\MicrosoftEdgeUpdateTaskMachineCore_20260513_081422', confirming the persistence mechanism is active. Wazuh rule 92760 re-fired on the 4702 event. The 2m46s gap between creation (08:14:22) and verification (08:17:08) is consistent with human-operator or scripted post-deployment confirmation.",
      "chain_reason": "EID 4702 on the same task name, same agent WIN-ENDPOINT-07, same user context. The create→query workflow is the attacker confirming persistence before proceeding to the next attack phase.",
      "first_seen": "2026-05-13T08:17:08+0200"
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "tactic": "Persistence — Scheduled Task Execution (First Cycle)",
      "technique": "T1053.005",
      "what_happened": "At 2026-05-13T08:19:22+0200 (first 5-minute task cycle from creation at 08:14:22), Sysmon EID 1 (Process Create) logged powershell.exe spawned by svchost.exe with parentCommandLine 'C:\\Windows\\System32\\svchost.exe -k netsvcs -p -s Schedule'. The commandLine contained -EncodedCommand, -NoProfile, -NonInteractive, and -WindowStyle Hidden flags. The decoded payload attempted Test-NetConnection to 10.108.57.184 port 443 — internal red-team C2 simulation address. This is the first task-cycle execution, confirming the scheduled task ran as designed and the encoded payload decoded and executed.",
      "chain_reason": "Sysmon EID 1: image=powershell.exe + parentImage=svchost.exe (Task Scheduler service host) + commandLine containing -EncodedCommand + -WindowStyle Hidden. The svchost.exe parentImage is the definitive signature of Windows Task Scheduler launching a process — distinguishes attacker task execution from interactive PowerShell.",
